<title>THAILAND: Thai sugar output passes 3.0 mln tonnes level.</title>
<headline>Thai sugar output passes 3.0 mln tonnes level.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai sugar production reached 3.34 million tonnes as cane crushing reached mid-season but the yield was still lower compared with last year's, an industry ministry source said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Thai mills had crushed 33.37 million tonnes of sugar cane as of February 18 to produce 2.0 million tonnes of raw sugar and 1.3 million tonnes of whites.</p>
<p>The sugar yield edged up to 99.08 kg per a tonne of sugar cane versus 98.17 kg last week but trailed the 103.62 kg recorded in the corresponding period last year.</p>
<p>Molasses production amounted to 1.38 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Thailand's 1996/97 crushing season started late in November and is expected to last until May or early June.</p>
<p>The following is the comparison of this season's sugar cane crushing details with the same period in the last season (in tonnes unless otherwise specified):</p>
<p>				   Feb 18, 1997	     Feb 18, 1996</p>
<p>Crushed sugar cane	    33,771,328		 33,280,175</p>
<p>Raw sugar			  1,998,152		  2,021,554</p>
<p>White and refined sugar	1,347,833		  1,426,972</p>
<p>Yield				    99.08		     103.62</p>
<p>Commercial Cane Sugar (pct)	11.29			11.87</p>
<p>Molasses			   1,389,257		  1,485,453</p>
<p>Yield				    41.14			44.63</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newroom (662) 652-0642</p>
